ms). A cached fit is reused,\\n6: never recomputed; files are written under a temporary name and\\n7: ``os.replace``d into place.\\n8: \\n9: A fit can run in a spawned child process with a time limit (agent-written\\n10: candidates: a pathological model must not stall the loop). Failures are\\n11: classified as in the PyMC domain: a failure of the model itself (its own\\n12: code raised, memo refused to compile it, it broke the contract, it gives an\\n13: observed choice probability zero) is a `ModelFailure` the caller turns into a\\n14: rejection; anything else (a killed worker, an unreadable file, OSError,\\n15: MemoryError) is infrastructure and raises.\\n16: \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n17: \\n18: from __future__ import annotations\\n19: \\n20: import hashlib\\n21: import json\\n22: import multiprocessing as mp\\n23: import os\\n24: import traceback\\n25: from dataclasses import asdict, dataclass\\n26: from pathlib import Path\\n27: from typing import Any, List, Optional\\n28: \\n29: from src.rsa.fit import FitSettings, RSAFit, ZeroProbabilityChoice\\n30: \\n31: FIT_TIME_LIMIT_SEC = 30 * 60  # as the PyMC domain's CANDIDATE_FIT_TIME_LIMIT_SEC\\n32: \\n33: \\n34: class ModelFailure(RuntimeError):\\n35:     \\\"\\\"\\\"The model failed (a rejection), as opposed to the infrastructure.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n36: \\n37: \\n38: class FitTimeLimitExceeded(ModelFailure):\\n39:     \\\"\\\"\\\"The fit ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n103: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1791346199310,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eeb753660ffeoSxUa5mxs618zH\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1148dcae6001e1Hwv5ofaOqBeW\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1148dc027001F4olcqiNPgxIIS\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eeb753660ffeoSxUa5mxs618zH\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":82859,\"input\":2451,\"output\":40,\"reasoning\":39,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":80329}},\"cost\":0.008159175}}\n104: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1791346201576,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eeb753660ffeoSxUa5mxs618zH\",\"part\":{\"i