{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791346374467,"sessionID":"ses_eeb753877ffeEZ5M2IaWa5Y4aK","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"UZAUi1wQabj923c5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/user/auto-psych/docs/auto_rsa/HANDOFF_smoke_test_2.md"},"output":"<path>/home/user/auto-psych/docs/auto_rsa/HANDOFF_smoke_test_2.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Handoff: RSA loop smoke test 2 (Gemini 3.8 Flash, all data, two rounds)\n2: \n3: **Goal.** The last check before Sherlock. Smoke test 1 (`SMOKE_RESULTS.md`)\n4: showed agents can get memo models admitted, but these were never exercised:\n5: \n6: - a self-check that finishes and that agents read;\n7: - a rejection followed by a repair;\n8: - Gemini 3.8 Flash (now the RSA default);\n9: - the external data download;\n10: - the larger combined dataset;\n11: - the new pruning unit.\n12: \n13: This run exercises all of them.\n14: \n15: **Where.** A fresh claude.ai cloud session on branch `auto-rsa`, in a\n16: disposable container, so `--no-sandbox` is acceptable here and nowhere else.\n17: `GOOGLE_API_KEY` must be set (check with `[ -n \"$GOOGLE_API_KEY\" ] && echo set`;\n18: never print it).\n19: \n20: ## Steps\n21: \n22: ```bash\n23: git checkout auto-rsa && git pull && uv sync\n24: npm i -g opencode-ai@1.18.35\n25: export GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=\"$GOOGLE_API_KEY\"\n26: cd /tmp && opencode run -m google/gemini-3.8-flash \"Reply with the word ok.\" ; cd -\n27: \n28: # 1. The data download (another failure mode on a fresh machine). It fetches\n29: #    the three sources without a licence from their pinned URLs, checks each\n30: #    sha256 and rebuilds the CSVs.\n31: uv run python -m src.rsa.ingest.run --sources mayn_demberg_2026 mayn_demberg_2023 mayn_demberg_2022 sikos_2021\n32: RSA_INGEST_FETCH=1 uv run pytest -q tests/test_rsa_ingest_*.py   # must pass; byte-identical rebuilds\n33: uv run python -m src.rsa.ingest.combine \\\n34:     --sources pragmods mayn_demberg_2026 mayn_demberg_2023 mayn_demberg_2022 sikos_2021 \\\n35:     --out data/rsa/combined_trials.csv\n36: \n37: # 2. The loop: 2 rounds x 3 slots on all five sources, with the RSA defaults\n38: #    (google/gemini-3.8-flash, 2,400 s per agent). Expect a few hours: the\n39: #    seed fits on about 50k forced-choice trials are slower than on pragmods.\n40: uv run python -m src.rsa.loop.run --results data/rsa/loop_smoke2 \\\n41:     --responses data/rsa/combined_trials.csv \\\n42:     --max-iterations 2 --candidate-count 3 --no-sandbox \\\n43:     --num-warmup 500 --num-samples 500 --num-chains 2\n44: ```\n45: \n46: If the seed fits on the combined data take over about 45 minutes, record the\n47: time per model (that number sizes the Sherlock job), then fall back to\n48: pragmods plus `mayn_demberg_2026` for the agent rounds and say so.\n49: \n50: ## What to report (in `docs/auto_rsa/SMOKE_RESULTS_2.md`)\n51: \n52: - **Download.** Did every source fetch and rebuild byte-identically? How long\n53:   did it take?\n54: - **Fit times.** Per seed model on the combined data (this sizes Sherlock\n55:   jobs), and per admission fit.\n56: - **Per slot.**\n57:   - Outcome and the exact rejection reason.\n58:   - Whether the self-check finished and the agent read its PASS/FAIL line.\n59:   - Any repair, and whether it succeeded.\n60:   - Memo errors hit.\n61:   - Tokens and wall time (from `token_usage.jsonl`).\n62:   - Gemini 3.8 Flash latency (first tool call).\n63: - **Round 2.** Does it see round 1's admitted models in its briefs and build\n64:   on them? Any convergence of the slots on one idea?\n65: - **The end-of-run prune.** What was pruned, and at what clustered-SE ratio?\n66: - **Disk.**\n67:   - Confirm no `.xdg_data/opencode/snapshot` directories (snapshots are now\n68:     off in `opencode.json`).\n69:   - Report the run directory's total size.\n70: - **Bugs.** Any bug that blocks the run: fix it with a test if it is small and\n71:   clear, and describe it.\n72: \n73: Commit the results document, any fix, and the small outputs to branch\n74: `auto-rsa-smoke2`. Small outputs means report.html, report.bundle.json,\n75: history.json, attempted_hypotheses.jsonl, token usage, and each candidate's\n76: hypothesis.md, model_name.txt and candidate.py. Leave out .fit_cache,\n77: responses.csv and the external cache. Do not push to `auto-rsa` or `main`,\n78: and do not open a pull request.\n\n(End of file - total 78 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Handoff: RSA loop smoke test 2 (Gemini 3.8 Flash, all data, two rounds)\n\n**Goal.** The last check before Sherlock. Smoke test 1 (`SMOKE_RESULTS.md`)\nshowed agents can get memo models admitted, but these were never exercised:\n\n- a self-check that finishes and that agents read;\n- a rejection followed by a repair;\n- Gemini 3.8 Flash (now the RSA default);\n- the external data download;\n- the larger combined dataset;\n- the new pruning unit.\n\nThis run exercises all of them.\n\n**Where.** A fresh claude.ai cloud session on branch `auto-rsa`, in a\ndisposable container, so `--no-sandbox` is acceptable here and nowhere else.\n`GOOGLE_API_KEY` must be set (check with `[ -n \"$GOOGLE_API_KEY\" ] && echo set`;\nnever print it).\n\n## Steps","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/user/auto-psych/docs/auto_rsa/HANDOFF_smoke_test_2.md","text":"# Handoff: RSA loop smoke test 2 (Gemini 3.8 Flash, all data, two rounds)\n\n**Goal.** The last check before Sherlock. Smoke test 1 (`SMOKE_RESULTS.md`)\nshowed agents can get memo models admitted, but these were never exercised:\n\n- a self-check that finishes and that agents read;\n- a rejection followed by a repair;\n- Gemini 3.8 Flash (now the RSA default);\n- the external data download;\n- the larger combined dataset;\n- the new pruning unit.\n\nThis run exercises all of them.\n\n**Where.** A fresh claude.ai cloud session on branch `auto-rsa`, in a\ndisposable container, so `--no-sandbox` is acceptable here and nowhere else.\n`GOOGLE_API_KEY` must be set (check with `[ -n \"$GOOGLE_API_KEY\" ] && echo set`;\nnever print it).\n\n## Steps\n\n```bash\ngit checkout auto-rsa && git pull && uv sync\nnpm i -g opencode-ai@1.18.35\nexport GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=\"$GOOGLE_API_KEY\"\ncd /tmp && opencode run -m google/gemini-3.8-flash \"Reply with the word ok.\" ; cd -\n\n# 1. The data download (another failure mode on a fresh machine). It fetches\n#    the three sources without a licence from their pinned URLs, checks each\n#    sha256 and rebuilds the CSVs.\nuv run python -m src.rsa.ingest.run --sources mayn_demberg_2026 mayn_demberg_2023 mayn_demberg_2022 sikos_2021\nRSA_INGEST_FETCH=1 uv run pytest -q tests/test_rsa_ingest_*.py   # must pass; byte-identical rebuilds\nuv run python -m src.rsa.ingest.combine \\\n    --sources pragmods mayn_demberg_2026 mayn_demberg_2023 mayn_demberg_2022 sikos_2021 \\\n    --out data/rsa/combined_trials.csv\n\n# 2. The loop: 2 rounds x 3 slots on all five sources, with the RSA defaults\n#    (google/gemini-3.8-flash, 2,400 s per agent). Expect a few hours: the\n#    seed fits on about 50k forced-choice trials are slower than on pragmods.\nuv run python -m src.rsa.loop.run --results data/rsa/loop_smoke2 \\\n    --responses data/rsa/combined_trials.csv \\\n    --max-iterations 2 --candidate-count 3 --no-sandbox \\\n    --num-warmup 500 --num-samples 500 --num-chains 2\n```\n\nIf the seed fits on the combined data take over about 45 minutes, record the\ntime per model (that number sizes the Sherlock job), then fall back to\npragmods plus `mayn_demberg_2026` for the agent rounds and say so.\n\n## What to report (in `docs/auto_rsa/SMOKE_RESULTS_2.md`)\n\n- **Download.** Did every source fetch and rebuild byte-identically? How long\n  did it take?\n- **Fit times.** Per seed model on the combined data (this sizes Sherlock\n  jobs), and per admission fit.\n- **Per slot.**\n  - Outcome and the exact rejection reason.\n  - Whether the self-check finished and the agent read its PASS/FAIL line.\n  - Any repair, and whether it succeeded.\n  - Memo errors hit.\n  - Tokens and wall time (from `token_usage.jsonl`).\n  - Gemini 3.8 Flash latency (first tool call).\n- **Round 2.** Does it see round 1's admitted models in its briefs and build\n  on them? Any convergence of the slots on one idea?\n- **The end-of-run prune.** What was pruned, and at what clustered-SE ratio?\n- **Disk.**\n  - Confirm no `.xdg_data/opencode/snapshot` directories (snapshots are now\n    off in `opencode.json`).\n  - Report the run directory's total size.\n- **Bugs.** Any bug that blocks the run: fix it with a test if it is small and\n  clear, and describe it.\n\nCommit the results document, any fix, and the small outputs to branch\n`auto-rsa-smoke2`. Small outputs means report.html, report.bundle.json,\nhistory.json, attempted_hypotheses.jsonl, token usage, and each candidate's\nhypothesis.md, model_name.txt and candidate.py. Leave out .fit_cache,\nresponses.csv and the external cache. Do not push to `auto-rsa` or `main`,\nand do not open a pull request.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":78,"totalLines":78,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/auto_rsa/HANDOFF_smoke_test_2.md","time":{"start":1791346374312,"end":1791346374429}},"metadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}},"id":"prt_11490769e001fGxpDtsN2ZWeJI","sessionID":"ses_eeb753877ffeEZ5M2IaWa5Y4aK","messageID":"msg_114906aad0012OAIVh55xZDteo"}}
